{"groups":[{"members":["c1"],"primary":"c1","title":"New Jersey cap on residential rental application fees ($50, CPI-adjusted)","requirement":"A landlord or agent may not charge an application or similar fee above $50 to apply to lease or sublease residential rental property for dwelling purposes. The Director of the Division of Consumer Affairs raises the cap each January 1 by any positive annual change in the CPI-U (New York-Northern New Jersey-Long Island) and publishes the current cap on the Division's website.","key_value":"$50 maximum application fee, adjusted annually for CPI","status":"in_force","effective_date":"2026-05-01","end_date":null,"citation":"P.L.2025, c.405 (N.J.S.A. 46:8-18.1)","coverage_conditions":"Applies statewide to applications to lease or sublease residential rental property for dwelling purposes.","exemptions":"Does not apply to a dwelling unit in a one-family or two-family dwelling offered for rent. Does not apply to a New Jersey Real Estate Commission licensee unless the licensee is the landlord of the property.","conflict_note":null},{"members":["c2"],"primary":"c2","title":"Mobile home parks: prohibition on entrance fees and required donations","requirement":"A landlord or operator of a mobile home park or private residential leasehold community may not require an entrance fee or other payment, including a donation or gift, from a person seeking to rent a space. A violation makes the landlord or operator a disorderly person, and the payer may recover double the amount paid plus losses in Superior Court.","key_value":"No entrance fee or other payment to rent a space in a park/community","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8C-2","coverage_conditions":"Mobile home parks and private residential leasehold communities.","exemptions":null,"conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
